{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"646bc48e1da36d61","type":"text","text":"# Week 5 — Writing Session\n\n## IELTS Writing Task 1: Line Graph — Sports & Exercise Trends\n\n**Level:** B1–B2  \n**Duration:** 2 hours  \n**Main skill:** Describing trends, comparisons, and overall patterns  \n**Topic:** Sports participation / exercise habits / public health  \n**Main outcome:** Students write one complete IELTS Task 1 line graph report in class.\n\n# Teaching Principle\n\nThis session follows:\n\n> Short input → sentence formation → data-to-sentence drill → paragraph building → full Task 1 report\n\nTeacher should not spend too much time explaining grammar.  \nThe main goal is to make students **look at data, choose key trends, and write accurate sentences**.\n\nSuggested ratio:\n\n|Role|Time|\n|---|--:|\n|Teacher talking|20–25%|\n|Student writing / correcting / discussing|75–80%|\n\n# Lesson Flow\n\n|Time|Stage|Purpose|\n|--:|---|---|\n|0–10 mins|Warm-up data talk|Activate trend language|\n|10–25 mins|Task 1 structure input|Understand intro, overview, details|\n|25–45 mins|Trend sentence drill|Build natural data sentences|\n|45–65 mins|Comparison drill|Compare lines accurately|\n|65–75 mins|Report planning|Choose overview + group data|\n|75–85 mins|Break||\n|85–110 mins|Guided full report writing|Students write complete Task 1 report|\n|110–120 mins|Fast feedback|Correct key errors|\n\n# 1. Lesson Objectives\n\nBy the end of the lesson, students can:\n\n|Skill|Outcome|\n|---|---|\n|Understand line graphs|Identify start, end, highest, lowest, and major changes|\n|Write introduction|Paraphrase the task clearly|\n|Write overview|Summarize main trends without numbers overload|\n|Describe details|Use data accurately with trend verbs|\n|Compare data|Use while, whereas, compared with, followed by|\n|Avoid common errors|Avoid “the number was increased” and “it was fluctuated”|\n\n# 2. Main Task\n\n## IELTS Task 1 Question\n\n> The table shows the percentage of people who did regular exercise in three age groups in one country between 2010 and 2025.  \n> Summarize the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\n\n## Data Table for Class Use\n\n|Year|16–24 age group|25–44 age group|45–64 age group|\n|--:|--:|--:|--:|\n|2010|52%|38%|25%|\n|2015|48%|42%|30%|\n|2020|55%|47%|36%|\n|2025|60%|50%|42%|\n\n# 3. Stage 1 — Warm-up Data Talk\n\n## 0–10 mins\n\nStudents look at the table and answer quickly in pairs.\n\n## Questions\n\n1. Which group had the highest exercise rate in 2010?\n    \n2. Which group had the lowest exercise rate in 2010?\n    \n3. Did all groups increase by 2025?\n    \n4. Which group increased the most?\n    \n5. Which group was the most stable?\n    \n6. What is the overall trend?\n    \n\n## Teacher Board Output\n\nExpected ideas:\n\n|Observation|Data|\n|---|---|\n|Young people were always the most active|52% → 60%|\n|Older adults had the lowest rate|25% → 42%|\n|All groups increased overall|2010 to 2025|\n|The 45–64 group rose the most|+17 percentage points|\n|16–24 dipped first, then recovered|52% → 48% → 60%|\n\n# 4. Stage 2 — Task 1 Structure Input\n\n## 10–25 mins\n\nKeep input short. Students need the structure, not a long lecture.\n\n# IELTS Task 1 Line Graph Structure\n\n|Paragraph|Purpose|What to write|\n|---|---|---|\n|Paragraph 1|Introduction|Paraphrase the chart|\n|Paragraph 2|Overview|Main trends, highest / lowest, overall pattern|\n|Paragraph 3|Details 1|Describe first group or similar lines|\n|Paragraph 4|Details 2|Describe remaining group / comparison|\n\n# Simple Formula\n\n> Introduction → Overview → Details 1 → Details 2\n\n# What Makes a Good Overview?\n\nA good overview should answer:\n\n1. What changed overall?\n    \n2. Which category was highest?\n    \n3. Which category was lowest?\n    \n4. Any special pattern?\n    \n\n## Weak Overview\n\n> Overall, the data changed a lot.\n\nProblem: too vague.\n\n## Better Overview\n\n> Overall, the proportion of people doing regular exercise increased in all three age groups. The youngest group remained the most active throughout the period, while the oldest group had the lowest figures but experienced the fastest growth.\n\n# 5. Native Sentence Frames for Task 1\n\n## 25–45 mins\n\n# A. Introduction Frames\n\n|Function|Sentence Frame|\n|---|---|\n|Paraphrase graph|The line graph compares...|\n|Describe subject|The graph shows changes in...|\n|Include time|...over a 15-year period from 2010 to 2025.|\n|Include unit|The figures are given in percentages.|\n\n## Model Introduction\n\n> The line graph compares the percentage of people in three age groups who did regular exercise in one country from 2010 to 2025.\n\n# B. Overview Frames\n\n|Function|Sentence Frame|\n|---|---|\n|Overall trend|Overall, all three age groups saw an increase in...|\n|Highest group|The youngest group remained the most active throughout the period.|\n|Lowest group|The oldest group recorded the lowest figures.|\n|Fastest growth|However, the oldest group experienced the most significant growth.|\n|Special pattern|The figure for young adults dipped slightly before rising steadily.|\n\n## Model Overview\n\n> Overall, all three age groups saw an increase in regular exercise participation. The 16–24 group remained the most active throughout the period, while the 45–64 group had the lowest figures but showed the strongest growth.\n\n# C. Trend Verb Frames\n\n|Trend|Natural Sentence|\n|---|---|\n|tăng|The figure rose from 38% to 50%.|\n|tăng đều|The percentage increased steadily over the period.|\n|giảm nhẹ|The figure fell slightly from 52% to 48%.|\n|phục hồi|It then recovered to 55% in 2020.|\n|đạt mức cao nhất|It reached a peak of 60% in 2025.|\n|giữ ổn định|The figure remained relatively stable.|\n|vượt qua|It overtook another group in 2020.|\n|cao hơn|It was consistently higher than the other groups.|\n\n# D. Comparison Frames\n\n|Function|Sentence Frame|\n|---|---|\n|Compare two groups|The figure for A was higher than that for B.|\n|Contrast|While A increased sharply, B rose more gradually.|\n|Gap|The gap between A and B narrowed over time.|\n|Rank|A ranked first, followed by B and C.|\n|Similarity|Both groups followed an upward trend.|\n|Difference|By contrast, the youngest group experienced a slight decline at first.|\n\n# 6. Sentence Formation Drill\n\n## 25–45 mins\n\n## Activity 1 — Data to Sentence\n\nStudents convert data into sentences.\n\n### Data 1\n\n16–24 age group: 52% in 2010 → 48% in 2015\n\n## Model\n\n> The figure for the 16–24 age group fell slightly from 52% in 2010 to 48% in 2015.\n\n### Data 2\n\n25–44 age group: 38% in 2010 → 50% in 2025\n\n## Model\n\n> The proportion of people aged 25–44 who exercised regularly rose steadily from 38% to 50% over the period.\n\n### Data 3\n\n45–64 age group: 25% in 2010 → 42% in 2025\n\n## Model\n\n> The 45–64 age group experienced the fastest growth, increasing from 25% in 2010 to 42% in 2025.\n\n### Data 4\n\n16–24 group always highest\n\n## Model\n\n> The youngest group remained the most active throughout the period.\n\n### Data 5\n\n45–64 group always lowest\n\n## Model\n\n> The oldest group consistently recorded the lowest participation rate.\n\n# Activity 2 — Basic to IELTS Sentence\n\n|Basic Sentence|Better IELTS Sentence|\n|---|---|\n|Young people exercised the most.|The 16–24 age group remained the most active throughout the period.|\n|Old people exercised the least.|The 45–64 group consistently had the lowest exercise participation rate.|\n|The middle group increased.|The figure for the 25–44 group rose steadily from 38% to 50%.|\n|The youngest group went down then up.|The percentage for the youngest group dipped slightly before rising to a peak in 2025.|\n|All groups increased.|All three age groups experienced an overall upward trend.|\n|The old group increased fastest.|The oldest group showed the most significant growth over the period.|\n\n# 7. Comparison Drill\n\n## 45–65 mins\n\n## Activity: Compare Two Lines\n\nStudents write comparison sentences using:\n\n- while\n    \n- whereas\n    \n- compared with\n    \n- followed by\n    \n- the gap between\n    \n\n## Drill 1\n\nData:\n\n|Group|2010|2025|\n|---|--:|--:|\n|16–24|52%|60%|\n|45–64|25%|42%|\n\n## Model\n\n> The 16–24 group was consistently more active than the 45–64 group, although the gap between them narrowed from 27 percentage points in 2010 to 18 points in 2025.\n\n## Drill 2\n\nData:\n\n|Group|2010|2025|\n|---|--:|--:|\n|25–44|38%|50%|\n|45–64|25%|42%|\n\n## Model\n\n> While both groups saw increases, the 45–64 group grew more sharply, rising by 17 percentage points compared with 12 points for the 25–44 group.\n\n## Drill 3\n\nData:\n\n|Year|16–24|25–44|45–64|\n|--:|--:|--:|--:|\n|2025|60%|50%|42%|\n\n## Model\n\n> By 2025, the 16–24 group had the highest rate at 60%, followed by the 25–44 group at 50% and the 45–64 group at 42%.\n\n# 8. Report Planning\n\n## 65–75 mins\n\nStudents complete this planning table before writing.\n\n|Section|Notes|\n|---|---|\n|Introduction|What does the graph compare?|\n|Overview point 1|Did all groups increase or decrease?|\n|Overview point 2|Which group was highest / lowest?|\n|Detail paragraph 1|16–24 and 25–44 groups|\n|Detail paragraph 2|45–64 group + final comparison|\n\n## Suggested Plan\n\n|Paragraph|Main Content|\n|---|---|\n|Introduction|Percentage of people doing regular exercise by age group, 2010–2025|\n|Overview|All increased; youngest highest; oldest lowest but fastest growth|\n|Details 1|16–24 dipped then rose; 25–44 rose steadily|\n|Details 2|45–64 rose sharply; final 2025 ranking|\n\n# 9. Break\n\n## 75–85 mins\n\n# 10. Guided Full Report Writing\n\n## 85–110 mins\n\nStudents write one complete Task 1 report.\n\n## Writing Task\n\n> The line graph shows the percentage of people who did regular exercise in three age groups in one country between 2010 and 2025.  \n> Summarize the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant.\n\n## Required Structure\n\n|Paragraph|Requirement|\n|---|---|\n|Introduction|Paraphrase the question|\n|Overview|Main trends, no detailed numbers needed|\n|Details 1|Describe 16–24 and 25–44|\n|Details 2|Describe 45–64 and compare final figures|\n\n## Timed Writing Breakdown\n\n|Time|Task|\n|--:|---|\n|3 mins|Review data|\n|4 mins|Write introduction|\n|5 mins|Write overview|\n|8 mins|Write Details 1|\n|8 mins|Write Details 2|\n|2 mins|Check grammar and numbers|\n\n# 11. Full Model Report\n\n> The line graph compares the percentage of people in three age groups who did regular exercise in one country from 2010 to 2025.\n> \n> Overall, all three age groups experienced an increase in regular exercise participation over the period. The 16–24 group remained the most active throughout, while the 45–64 group recorded the lowest figures but showed the strongest growth.\n> \n> In 2010, 52% of people aged 16–24 did regular exercise, which was the highest figure on the graph. This percentage fell slightly to 48% in 2015, before recovering to 55% in 2020 and reaching a peak of 60% in 2025. Meanwhile, the figure for the 25–44 age group rose steadily from 38% in 2010 to 42% in 2015, then continued to increase to 47% in 2020 and 50% by the end of the period.\n> \n> The oldest age group had the lowest participation rate at the beginning, at only 25% in 2010. However, it increased consistently to 30% in 2015, 36% in 2020, and 42% in 2025. Although this group remained the least active, it experienced the largest overall rise, increasing by 17 percentage points.\n\n# 12. Why This Report Works\n\n|Feature|Example|\n|---|---|\n|Clear introduction|compares the percentage of people...|\n|Strong overview|all groups increased; youngest highest; oldest fastest growth|\n|Accurate data|52%, 48%, 55%, 60%|\n|Good comparison|youngest highest, oldest lowest|\n|Natural trend verbs|fell slightly, recovering, reaching a peak, rose steadily|\n|No opinion|No explanation like “because people care about health”|\n\n# 13. Fast Feedback\n\n## 110–120 mins\n\nTeacher collects 3–5 common mistakes and corrects them on the board.\n\n## Correction Priority\n\n|Priority|Check|\n|---|---|\n|1|Is there an overview?|\n|2|Are numbers accurate?|\n|3|Are trend verbs correct?|\n|4|Are comparisons clear?|\n|5|Is the report objective, with no personal opinion?|\n\n# 14. Common B1–B2 Errors\n\n|Student Error|Natural Correction|\n|---|---|\n|The graph illustrates about...|The graph illustrates...|\n|The number of people increased from 52% to 60%.|The percentage of people increased from 52% to 60%.|\n|It was increased.|It increased.|\n|It was fluctuated.|It fluctuated.|\n|The 16–24 was highest.|The 16–24 age group had the highest figure.|\n|The old people group was lowest.|The 45–64 age group recorded the lowest figure.|\n|In 2010 was 52%.|In 2010, the figure was 52%.|\n|It increased 38% to 50%.|It increased from 38% to 50%.|\n|It reached at 60%.|It reached 60%.|\n|Older people exercise more because they care about health.|Do not explain causes unless the chart gives reasons.|\n|Overall, there are many changes.|Overall, all three groups experienced an upward trend.|\n\n# 15. Natural Expression Bank\n\n## Introduction\n\n- The line graph compares...\n    \n- The graph shows changes in...\n    \n- The figures are given in percentages.\n    \n- ...over a 15-year period from 2010 to 2025.\n    \n\n## Overview\n\n- Overall, all three groups experienced an upward trend.\n    \n- The youngest group remained the most active throughout the period.\n    \n- The oldest group recorded the lowest figures.\n    \n- The most significant growth was seen in...\n    \n- Although it remained the lowest, it showed the strongest increase.\n    \n\n## Trend Verbs\n\n|Verb|Example|\n|---|---|\n|rise|The figure rose from 38% to 50%.|\n|increase|The percentage increased steadily.|\n|fall|The figure fell slightly in 2015.|\n|recover|It then recovered to 55%.|\n|reach|It reached a peak of 60%.|\n|remain|It remained the highest figure.|\n|experience|The group experienced the largest increase.|\n\n## Comparison\n\n- compared with...\n    \n- while...\n    \n- whereas...\n    \n- followed by...\n    \n- by contrast...\n    \n- the gap between A and B...\n    \n- higher than...\n    \n- lower than...\n    \n- the highest figure\n    \n- the lowest figure\n    \n\n# 16. Student Checklist Before Submission\n\n|Question|Yes / No|\n|---|---|\n|Did I write an introduction?||\n|Did I write a clear overview?||\n|Did I avoid personal opinions?||\n|Did I describe the main trends?||\n|Did I compare at least two groups?||\n|Did I use numbers accurately?||\n|Did I use “from...to...” correctly?||\n|Did I avoid “was increased / was fluctuated”?||\n\n# 17. Homework\n\n## Homework 1 — Rewrite the Report\n\nStudents rewrite the same report after correction.\n\nRequirements:\n\n|Requirement|Detail|\n|---|---|\n|Length|150–180 words|\n|Structure|4 paragraphs|\n|Must include|Introduction + overview|\n|Must include|At least 6 numbers|\n|Must include|At least 3 comparisons|\n|Must avoid|Personal opinion / explanation of causes|\n\n## Homework 2 — Sentence Practice\n\nWrite 10 sentences using these frames:\n\n1. The line graph compares...\n    \n2. Overall, all three groups...\n    \n3. The figure rose from...to...\n    \n4. The percentage fell slightly from...to...\n    \n5. It reached a peak of...\n    \n6. It remained the highest...\n    \n7. By contrast,...\n    \n8. While A increased..., B...\n    \n9. The gap between A and B...\n    \n10. By the end of the period,...\n    \n\n# 18. Optional Extra Task 1 Questions\n\nUse these for stronger students or future practice.\n\n## Question 1\n\n> The line graph shows the percentage of students who played football, basketball, and swimming from 2010 to 2025.\n\n## Question 2\n\n> The line graph compares gym membership rates among men and women between 2005 and 2020.\n\n## Question 3\n\n> The line graph shows the average number of hours people spent exercising each week in three age groups from 2010 to 2025.\n\n## Question 4\n\n> The line graph compares participation in outdoor sports and indoor sports over a 20-year period.\n\n# 19. Teacher Board Summary\n\n## Task 1 Line Graph\n\n> Do not explain why.  \n> Describe what the data shows.\n\n## Report Structure\n\n> Introduction → Overview → Details 1 → Details 2\n\n## Best Overview\n\n> Overall, all three groups increased, with the youngest group remaining the most active and the oldest group showing the fastest growth.\n\n## Best Sentence Frames\n\n1. The line graph compares...\n    \n2. Overall, all three age groups...\n    \n3. The figure rose from...to...\n    \n4. It fell slightly before recovering to...\n    \n5. The youngest group remained...\n    \n6. The oldest group recorded...\n    \n7. By the end of the period,...\n    \n8. Although..., it...\n    \n\n## Avoid\n\n- “The graph illustrates about...”\n    \n- “It was increased.”\n    \n- “It was fluctuated.”\n    \n- “The number was 52%.”\n    \n- giving reasons not shown in the graph\n    \n- writing details without overview","x":-600,"y":-480,"width":720,"height":29306},
