		{"id":"db7ec2a81e63b649","type":"text","text":"1. CO2 and sunlight are absorbed into plants and trees, helping them  grow up\n2. the corns are then harvested and transport to be pre-processed in into cellulose.\n3. these components are then continued to be processed - distilled until they become sugar particle \n4. these particle are then added / mixed with microbes, which turn them into ethanol.\n5. Ethanol are then mixed with gasoline and become reliable, sustainable fuel for commercial use, which inturn release CO2 back to the environment, ready to be consumed by new crops again.\n","x":3744,"y":1920,"width":250,"height":686},
